===Etymology 1===
{{etymid|fi|northwest}}
From {{inh|fi|urj-fin-pro|*loodëh|id=direction}} (compare {{cog|et|loe}}, {{cog|izh|looe}}, {{m|izh|loove}}, {{cog|krl|luuveh||west; southwest}}, {{cog|liv|lūod}}, {{cog|lud|luodeh||west}}, {{cog|vep|lode||northwest; west}}, {{m|vep|lodeh||northwest; west}}, {{cog|vot|looõ||northwest, west}}), of uncertain further origin; theories include relation to {{m|fi|luoda}} and {{m|fi|luo}} (possibly a verb with like {{m|fi||*luotaa|to descend}}) and relation to etymology 2 (Germanic origin).<ref>{{R:et:EES|loe}}</ref>

