===Etymology 2===
{{etymid|fi|ebb}}
From {{inh|fi|urj-fin-pro|*loodëh|id=tide}}, borrowed from {{der|fi|gem-pro|*flōduz}} (compare {{cog|de|Flut}}, {{cog|sv|flod}}) and derived with {{suffix|fi||-e}}. Originally meant flood or high tide; the sense "ebb" is a literary invention from the 1830s. See also {{m|fi|vuoksi}} for further details.

